# Practical No. 8(A)

## Aim
To style a React component using CSS Modules for component-specific styling.

## Code

### `src/App.js`

```jsx
import React from "react";
import StyledCard from "./components/StyledCard";

function App() {
  return <StyledCard />;
}

export default App;
```

### `src/components/StyledCard.jsx`

```jsx
import React from "react";
import styles from "./StyledCard.module.css";

function StyledCard() {
  return (
    <div className={styles.card}>
      <h2>React CSS Module</h2>
      <p>This style is scoped to the component.</p>
    </div>
  );
}

export default StyledCard;
```

### `src/components/StyledCard.module.css`

```css
.card {
  width: 400px;
  margin: 30px auto;
  padding: 25px;
  border: 1px solid #cccccc;
  border-radius: 10px;
  text-align: center;
}
```

## Output

A centered card displaying **React CSS Module** and the text *This style is scoped to the component.*, styled with a border, rounded corners, and padding.

## Result
Successfully styled a React component using CSS Modules with component-specific styling.
